# --- 11-04: the lagoon cave ---
# (11-04) A cave from the lagoon floor in front of the landing, under the ring and up into a sea stack in the bay past
# the reef: an underwater mouth by a sunken dinghy, the tunnel climbing out of the water, a dry den with air. Not under
# the shelter as first planned: the den is some 21 x 22 m and 11 m high at the least size, the lagoon 2-6 m deep and
# the shelter's rooms fill the islet. hill=0: no ridge over the lagoon (a ridge would fill the landing's water).
call kit_st x=-4 z=-22 yaw=205 len=35.6 slope=12 end=room size=0.7 hill=0 dirt=2 mush=2 stone=1 vines=1 as=shelcave
# (the dinghy in front of the mouth, off its right side and clear of the landing's deck; the mouth's sides are walled with two boulders on the cut's
# floor: hill=0 leaves the mouth piece's flanks bare where its approach is cut down, and a diver beside the mouth saw
# into the tunnel through the shell's back - X7, CICaveInside)
# (11-05: "ground sit" sat it on the landing deck's corner, up in the air over the water: dropped from under the surface
# onto the lagoon floor, sunk as the islanders' notes say)
# (11-05 round 2: it had dropped onto the mouth frame's rock, over a hollow; now on the lagoon floor east of the landing's
# pillars, keeled over and half in the sand as a wreck - RF1)
place RT_PlasticBoat dinghy at 0.5 -14.8 y=-0.5 sit yaw=150 tilt=14 roll=25
prop dinghy obj.name=dinghy
# (Raft's grey boulders, not Temperance's snow-capped blue rock - it stood out navy blue on the lagoon's sand, 11-05)
place SmallBoulder3 - at -11.5 -19.6 ground sit scale=0.65 yaw=40
# (and one close by the mouth's right lip: from inside the mouth a slit beside it looked out through the shell's back)
place SmallBoulder3 - at -7.9 -19.5 ground sit scale=0.65 yaw=100
place SmallBoulder3 - at 2.65 -26.2 ground sit scale=0.65 yaw=160
# (the mouth piece's shell back, seen from beside the frame's west flank: 21 open spots - a big boulder over it, RF2;
# a second at -6.8 -26 stood in the tunnel's way down)
# (on the very spot CICaveInside stands at, -7.9 -22.7: one beside it left the look free)
place SmallBoulder3 - at -8.1 -22.8 ground y=-0.3 sit scale=1.7 yaw=20
# (a palm the den's rock grew round stood out of the sea stack's side, its crown inside: cleared)
clear at -23.6 -64 r=16 all body only=Tree
place Zone_Trigger shelair at -23.6 -64 h=3.6
prop shelair obj.name=shelair
prop shelair zone.id=shelair
prop shelair zone.radius=7
prop shelair zone.repeat=1
prop shelair zone.air=1
prop shelair zone.message=A dry cave in the sea rock - air. The expedition camped here.
# cavecheck inside shelsupply
place Loot_ChestSmall shelsupply at -26 -66.5 h=6 drop yaw=25
prop shelsupply obj.name=shelsupply
prop shelsupply beh.hidden=1
prop shelsupply loot.refill=0
note shelsupply Expedition supply chest | The Abyss Expedition's chest, left in the dry cave for the divers: air, water and salve.
loot shelsupply OxygenBottle*2;PlasticBottle_Water*2;HealingSalve_Good*1;Rope*2
# --- 11-05: cave rats (the user: "in some caves there can be a monster, like a rat") ---
# Tangaroa rats, not Raft's rats: the quest's "Clear the rats out of the dormitory" counts animals labelled Rat, and
# rats killed in a cave must not count for the dormitory. On the cave's floor, 6 m and more from the chests
# and off the way in. No respawn.
# (11-06 review: Radar Hill's planting (ar_plants_hill at 60 54 r=22) put palms under the ammo cave's rock, at its back
# where the rats live - no trees under rock: taken out of the cave)
clear at 62 80 r=11 all only=Palm|Tree|Bamboo|Banana|Mango below=9
# The ammo cave: two at its back, 12 m from its chest by the mouth (the same den as The Abyss's lava tube). The lagoon cave's den is reached only under water and gets no NavMesh floor: no rats there
place Creature_Rat_Tangaroa ammorats at 63 75 h=4.5
prop ammorats creature.count=2
prop ammorats creature.respawn=0
save Shelter Atoll
